{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Lit table with the columns and data that are unique to that table."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header render helpers, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable render helpers only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/basic-app-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic App Table"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Minimal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" setup."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/composable-tables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Composable Tables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Richer Users and Products tables sharing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/hooks/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" and reusable render helpers."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"start-with-shared-features-and-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start With Shared Features and Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { useAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" become defaults for every table created by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"features"},{"type":"text","value":" option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-app-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create App Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof features"},{"type":"text","value":" through its column definitions."}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"create-a-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create A Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create each table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":". The call site provides table-specific inputs such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":"; shared features and defaults come from the hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"private appTable = (() => {\n  const host = this\n  return useAppTable(\n    this,\n    {\n      columns,\n      get data() {\n        return host.data\n      },\n    },\n    (state) => ({ sorting: state.sorting }),\n  )\n})()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-with-the-normal-table-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render With The Normal Table APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableController"},{"type":"text","value":" table. This simple path does not require "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppCell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppHeader"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AppFooter"},{"type":"text","value":", or registered render helpers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const table = this.appTable.table()\n\nreturn html`\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n        (headerGroup) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${headerGroup.headers.map(\n              (header) => html`\n                <th @click=${header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                  ${header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })}\n                </th>\n              `,\n            )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n        (row) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${row\n              .getAllCells()\n              .map((cell) => html`<td>${FlexRender({ cell })}</td>`)}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"override-shared-defaults-per-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override Shared Defaults Per Table"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":" override defaults from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":". Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const host = this\n\nconst table = useAppTable(this, {\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return host.data\n  },\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optional-reusable-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional: Reusable Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The richer composable-tables example also uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-registry-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Registry Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The composable tables example keeps the shared configuration in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/hooks/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from '../components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from '../components/header-components'\n\nexport const features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const { createAppColumnHelper, useAppTable, useTableContext } =\n  createTableHook({\n    features,\n    getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n    cellComponents: {\n      TextCell,\n      NumberCell,\n      StatusCell,\n      ProgressCell,\n      RowActionsCell,\n      PriceCell,\n      CategoryCell,\n    },\n    headerComponents: {\n      SortIndicator,\n      ColumnFilter,\n      FooterColumnId,\n      FooterSum,\n    },\n  })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Lit example does not register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":". Its table-level controls are custom elements that call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTableContext(this)"},{"type":"text","value":", so they consume table context directly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"returned-helpers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returned Helpers"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableController"},{"type":"text","value":"-backed app table for a Lit host and attaches app render helpers."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates column helpers with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" and registered cell/header component types already bound."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTableContext"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lets custom elements like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pagination-controls"},{"type":"text","value":" read the nearest app table context."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create one column helper per row type. Cell/header components in Lit are functions, so column definitions call the registered function on the enhanced "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.TextCell(),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.NumberCell(),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.RowActionsCell(),\n  }),\n])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"component-table-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component Table Rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable(this, options, selector)"},{"type":"text","value":" from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitElement"},{"type":"text","value":" host. The helper returns an object with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table()"},{"type":"text","value":", which computes the current app table through the controller."}]},{"type":"code","value":"private appTable = (() => {\n  const host = this\n  return useAppTable(\n    this,\n    {\n      columns,\n      get data() {\n        return host.data\n      },\n      debugTable: true,\n    },\n    (state) => ({\n      pagination: state.pagination,\n      sorting: state.sorting,\n      columnFilters: state.columnFilters,\n    }),\n  )\n})()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render()"},{"type":"text","value":", use callback-based app wrappers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const table = this.appTable.table()\n\nreturn html`\n  <table-toolbar .title=${'Users Table'}></table-toolbar>\n\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n        (headerGroup) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${headerGroup.headers.map((h) =>\n              table.AppHeader(\n                h,\n                (header) => html`\n                  <th @click=${header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                    ${header.FlexRender()} ${header.SortIndicator()}\n                    ${header.ColumnFilter()}\n                  </th>\n                `,\n              ),\n            )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n        (row) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${row\n              .getAllCells()\n              .map((cell) =>\n                table.AppCell(\n                  cell,\n                  (appCell) => html`<td>${appCell.FlexRender()}</td>`,\n                ),\n              )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n  <pagination-controls></pagination-controls>\n  <row-count></row-count>\n`","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reusing-the-component-registry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reusing The Component Registry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Users and Products table elements import the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppColumnHelper"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAppTable"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/hooks/table.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". Their data and columns differ, but sorting, filtering, pagination, row IDs, and registered cell/header renderers come from one shared configuration."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-this-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When To Use This Pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableController"},{"type":"text","value":" API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"start-with-shared-features-and-options","text":"Start With Shared Features and Options","level":2},{"id":"create-app-columns","text":"Create App Columns","level":2},{"id":"create-a-table","text":"Create A Table","level":2},{"id":"render-with-the-normal-table-apis","text":"Render With The Normal Table APIs","level":2},{"id":"override-shared-defaults-per-table","text":"Override Shared Defaults Per Table","level":2},{"id":"optional-reusable-components","text":"Optional: Reusable Components","level":2},{"id":"component-registry-setup","text":"Component Registry Setup","level":3},{"id":"returned-helpers","text":"Returned Helpers","level":3},{"id":"component-columns","text":"Component Columns","level":3},{"id":"component-table-rendering","text":"Component Table Rendering","level":3},{"id":"reusing-the-component-registry","text":"Reusing The Component Registry","level":3},{"id":"when-to-use-this-pattern","text":"When To Use This Pattern","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`createTableHook` creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Lit table with the columns and data that are unique to that table.\n\nThe same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header render helpers, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable render helpers only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces.\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic App Table](../examples/basic-app-table) - Minimal `createTableHook` setup.\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables) - Richer Users and Products tables sharing `src/hooks/table.ts` and reusable render helpers.\n\n## Start With Shared Features and Options\n\nCreate one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by `useAppTable`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { useAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})\n```\n\nOptions passed to `createTableHook` become defaults for every table created by `useAppTable`. The `features` option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available.\n\n## Create App Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread `typeof features` through its column definitions.\n\n```ts\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n## Create A Table\n\nCreate each table with `useAppTable`. The call site provides table-specific inputs such as `columns` and `data`; shared features and defaults come from the hook.\n\n```ts\nprivate appTable = (() => {\n  const host = this\n  return useAppTable(\n    this,\n    {\n      columns,\n      get data() {\n        return host.data\n      },\n    },\n    (state) => ({ sorting: state.sorting }),\n  )\n})()\n```\n\n## Render With The Normal Table APIs\n\nYou can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone `TableController` table. This simple path does not require `AppCell`, `AppHeader`, `AppFooter`, or registered render helpers.\n\n```ts\nconst table = this.appTable.table()\n\nreturn html`\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n        (headerGroup) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${headerGroup.headers.map(\n              (header) => html`\n                <th @click=${header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                  ${header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })}\n                </th>\n              `,\n            )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n        (row) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${row\n              .getAllCells()\n              .map((cell) => html`<td>${FlexRender({ cell })}</td>`)}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n`\n```\n\n## Override Shared Defaults Per Table\n\nOptions passed to `useAppTable` override defaults from `createTableHook`. Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook.\n\n```ts\nconst host = this\n\nconst table = useAppTable(this, {\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return host.data\n  },\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n})\n```\n\n## Optional: Reusable Components\n\nThe richer composable-tables example also uses `createTableHook` as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers.\n\n### Component Registry Setup\n\nThe composable tables example keeps the shared configuration in `src/hooks/table.ts`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from '../components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from '../components/header-components'\n\nexport const features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const { createAppColumnHelper, useAppTable, useTableContext } =\n  createTableHook({\n    features,\n    getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n    cellComponents: {\n      TextCell,\n      NumberCell,\n      StatusCell,\n      ProgressCell,\n      RowActionsCell,\n      PriceCell,\n      CategoryCell,\n    },\n    headerComponents: {\n      SortIndicator,\n      ColumnFilter,\n      FooterColumnId,\n      FooterSum,\n    },\n  })\n```\n\nThe Lit example does not register `tableComponents` in `createTableHook`. Its table-level controls are custom elements that call `useTableContext(this)`, so they consume table context directly.\n\n### Returned Helpers\n\n| Helper                  | Purpose                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useAppTable`           | Creates a `TableController`-backed app table for a Lit host and attaches app render helpers.      |\n| `createAppColumnHelper` | Creates column helpers with `TFeatures` and registered cell/header component types already bound. |\n| `useTableContext`       | Lets custom elements like `pagination-controls` read the nearest app table context.               |\n\n### Component Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. Cell/header components in Lit are functions, so column definitions call the registered function on the enhanced `cell` or `header`.\n\n```ts\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.TextCell(),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.NumberCell(),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.RowActionsCell(),\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n### Component Table Rendering\n\nCall `useAppTable(this, options, selector)` from the `LitElement` host. The helper returns an object with `table()`, which computes the current app table through the controller.\n\n```ts\nprivate appTable = (() => {\n  const host = this\n  return useAppTable(\n    this,\n    {\n      columns,\n      get data() {\n        return host.data\n      },\n      debugTable: true,\n    },\n    (state) => ({\n      pagination: state.pagination,\n      sorting: state.sorting,\n      columnFilters: state.columnFilters,\n    }),\n  )\n})()\n```\n\nInside `render()`, use callback-based app wrappers:\n\n```ts\nconst table = this.appTable.table()\n\nreturn html`\n  <table-toolbar .title=${'Users Table'}></table-toolbar>\n\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n        (headerGroup) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${headerGroup.headers.map((h) =>\n              table.AppHeader(\n                h,\n                (header) => html`\n                  <th @click=${header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                    ${header.FlexRender()} ${header.SortIndicator()}\n                    ${header.ColumnFilter()}\n                  </th>\n                `,\n              ),\n            )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n        (row) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${row\n              .getAllCells()\n              .map((cell) =>\n                table.AppCell(\n                  cell,\n                  (appCell) => html`<td>${appCell.FlexRender()}</td>`,\n                ),\n              )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n  <pagination-controls></pagination-controls>\n  <row-count></row-count>\n`\n```\n\n### Reusing The Component Registry\n\nThe Users and Products table elements import the same `createAppColumnHelper` and `useAppTable` from `src/hooks/table.ts`. Their data and columns differ, but sorting, filtering, pagination, row IDs, and registered cell/header renderers come from one shared configuration.\n\n## When To Use This Pattern\n\nUse `createTableHook` when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone `TableController` API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Composable Tables (createTableHook) Guide\n---\n\n`createTableHook` creates an app-specific table factory. Use it to define shared features, row models, and default table options once, then create each Lit table with the columns and data that are unique to that table.\n\nThe same API can also register reusable table, cell, and header render helpers, but component registration is optional. Start with shared options and features first; add reusable render helpers only when your app needs standardized table UI pieces.\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Basic App Table](../examples/basic-app-table) - Minimal `createTableHook` setup.\n- [Composable Tables](../examples/composable-tables) - Richer Users and Products tables sharing `src/hooks/table.ts` and reusable render helpers.\n\n## Start With Shared Features and Options\n\nCreate one app table hook and put the feature set, row models, and shared defaults there. This example makes sorting available to every table created by `useAppTable`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n})\n\nconst { useAppTable, createAppColumnHelper } = createTableHook({\n  features,\n  debugTable: true,\n  enableSortingRemoval: false,\n})\n```\n\nOptions passed to `createTableHook` become defaults for every table created by `useAppTable`. The `features` option is also bound to the returned column helper, so column definitions know that sorting APIs are available.\n\n## Create App Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. The helper is already bound to your app's feature set, so each table does not need to thread `typeof features` through its column definitions.\n\n```ts\ntype Person = {\n  firstName: string\n  lastName: string\n  age: number\n  visits: number\n}\n\nconst columnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = columnHelper.columns([\n  columnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor((row) => row.lastName, {\n    id: 'lastName',\n    header: 'Last Name',\n    cell: (info) => info.getValue(),\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n  }),\n  columnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n    header: 'Visits',\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n## Create A Table\n\nCreate each table with `useAppTable`. The call site provides table-specific inputs such as `columns` and `data`; shared features and defaults come from the hook.\n\n```ts\nprivate appTable = (() => {\n  const host = this\n  return useAppTable(\n    this,\n    {\n      columns,\n      get data() {\n        return host.data\n      },\n    },\n    (state) => ({ sorting: state.sorting }),\n  )\n})()\n```\n\n## Render With The Normal Table APIs\n\nYou can render the table with the same table instance APIs used by a standalone `TableController` table. This simple path does not require `AppCell`, `AppHeader`, `AppFooter`, or registered render helpers.\n\n```ts\nconst table = this.appTable.table()\n\nreturn html`\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n        (headerGroup) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${headerGroup.headers.map(\n              (header) => html`\n                <th @click=${header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                  ${header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })}\n                </th>\n              `,\n            )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n        (row) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${row\n              .getAllCells()\n              .map((cell) => html`<td>${FlexRender({ cell })}</td>`)}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n`\n```\n\n## Override Shared Defaults Per Table\n\nOptions passed to `useAppTable` override defaults from `createTableHook`. Use this for the few tables that need different behavior without creating a separate app hook.\n\n```ts\nconst host = this\n\nconst table = useAppTable(this, {\n  columns,\n  get data() {\n    return host.data\n  },\n  enableSortingRemoval: true,\n})\n```\n\n## Optional: Reusable Components\n\nThe richer composable-tables example also uses `createTableHook` as a component registry. Use this when several tables should share the same toolbar controls, cell renderers, header renderers, or footer renderers.\n\n### Component Registry Setup\n\nThe composable tables example keeps the shared configuration in `src/hooks/table.ts`.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  createFilteredRowModel,\n  createPaginatedRowModel,\n  createSortedRowModel,\n  createTableHook,\n  filterFns,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortFns,\n  tableFeatures,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\nimport {\n  CategoryCell,\n  NumberCell,\n  PriceCell,\n  ProgressCell,\n  RowActionsCell,\n  StatusCell,\n  TextCell,\n} from '../components/cell-components'\nimport {\n  ColumnFilter,\n  FooterColumnId,\n  FooterSum,\n  SortIndicator,\n} from '../components/header-components'\n\nexport const features = tableFeatures({\n  columnFilteringFeature,\n  rowPaginationFeature,\n  rowSortingFeature,\n  sortedRowModel: createSortedRowModel(),\n  filteredRowModel: createFilteredRowModel(),\n  paginatedRowModel: createPaginatedRowModel(),\n  sortFns,\n  filterFns,\n})\n\nexport const { createAppColumnHelper, useAppTable, useTableContext } =\n  createTableHook({\n    features,\n    getRowId: (row) => row.id,\n    cellComponents: {\n      TextCell,\n      NumberCell,\n      StatusCell,\n      ProgressCell,\n      RowActionsCell,\n      PriceCell,\n      CategoryCell,\n    },\n    headerComponents: {\n      SortIndicator,\n      ColumnFilter,\n      FooterColumnId,\n      FooterSum,\n    },\n  })\n```\n\nThe Lit example does not register `tableComponents` in `createTableHook`. Its table-level controls are custom elements that call `useTableContext(this)`, so they consume table context directly.\n\n### Returned Helpers\n\n| Helper                  | Purpose                                                                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `useAppTable`           | Creates a `TableController`-backed app table for a Lit host and attaches app render helpers.      |\n| `createAppColumnHelper` | Creates column helpers with `TFeatures` and registered cell/header component types already bound. |\n| `useTableContext`       | Lets custom elements like `pagination-controls` read the nearest app table context.               |\n\n### Component Columns\n\nCreate one column helper per row type. Cell/header components in Lit are functions, so column definitions call the registered function on the enhanced `cell` or `header`.\n\n```ts\nconst personColumnHelper = createAppColumnHelper<Person>()\n\nconst columns = personColumnHelper.columns([\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('firstName', {\n    header: 'First Name',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.TextCell(),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.accessor('age', {\n    header: 'Age',\n    footer: (props) => props.column.id,\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.NumberCell(),\n  }),\n  personColumnHelper.display({\n    id: 'actions',\n    header: 'Actions',\n    cell: ({ cell }) => cell.RowActionsCell(),\n  }),\n])\n```\n\n### Component Table Rendering\n\nCall `useAppTable(this, options, selector)` from the `LitElement` host. The helper returns an object with `table()`, which computes the current app table through the controller.\n\n```ts\nprivate appTable = (() => {\n  const host = this\n  return useAppTable(\n    this,\n    {\n      columns,\n      get data() {\n        return host.data\n      },\n      debugTable: true,\n    },\n    (state) => ({\n      pagination: state.pagination,\n      sorting: state.sorting,\n      columnFilters: state.columnFilters,\n    }),\n  )\n})()\n```\n\nInside `render()`, use callback-based app wrappers:\n\n```ts\nconst table = this.appTable.table()\n\nreturn html`\n  <table-toolbar .title=${'Users Table'}></table-toolbar>\n\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      ${table.getHeaderGroups().map(\n        (headerGroup) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${headerGroup.headers.map((h) =>\n              table.AppHeader(\n                h,\n                (header) => html`\n                  <th @click=${header.column.getToggleSortingHandler()}>\n                    ${header.FlexRender()} ${header.SortIndicator()}\n                    ${header.ColumnFilter()}\n                  </th>\n                `,\n              ),\n            )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      ${table.getRowModel().rows.map(\n        (row) => html`\n          <tr>\n            ${row\n              .getAllCells()\n              .map((cell) =>\n                table.AppCell(\n                  cell,\n                  (appCell) => html`<td>${appCell.FlexRender()}</td>`,\n                ),\n              )}\n          </tr>\n        `,\n      )}\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n  <pagination-controls></pagination-controls>\n  <row-count></row-count>\n`\n```\n\n### Reusing The Component Registry\n\nThe Users and Products table elements import the same `createAppColumnHelper` and `useAppTable` from `src/hooks/table.ts`. Their data and columns differ, but sorting, filtering, pagination, row IDs, and registered cell/header renderers come from one shared configuration.\n\n## When To Use This Pattern\n\nUse `createTableHook` when multiple tables should share features, row models, default options, or conventions. Use the standalone `TableController` API for a one-off table. Add the component registry only when the app wants standardized reusable table UI pieces.\n"}
